+typed arguments would emit `call i64 @nz.f1(i1 %a, i64 %b)`, clang would reject it, and
+the verdict would be UNUSABLE. A build failure is not evidence that an argument-order test
+discriminates — it is evidence that the IR was malformed, which is a different defect and
+one the tests below never had to catch.
+
+Caught by `arguments_are_not_swapped`, which uses noncommutative operations: `sub(10, 3)`
+is 7 and the transposition makes it -7. `mix(1, 2, 3)` catches a rotation as well.
+"""
+file = "crates/nazm-lir/src/emit.rs"
